{"p07:TF":{"cols":["kind","source","location","quote"],"rows":[["design","article.html","Abstract","we treated 104 genotyped segregants from a cross between two yeast strains with a collection of 100 diverse small molecules"],["count","article.html","Abstract","We used linkage analysis to identify 124 distinct linkages between genetic markers and response to 83 compounds"],["hotspots","article.html","Abstract","The linked markers clustered at eight genomic locations, or quantitative-trait locus 'hotspots', that contain one or more polymorphisms that affect response to multiple small molecules"],["candidate","article.html","Abstract","We also experimentally verified that a deficiency in leucine biosynthesis caused by a deletion of LEU2 underlies sensitivity to niguldipine"],["candidate","article.html","Abstract","a natural coding-region polymorphism in the inorganic phosphate transporter PHO84 underlies sensitivity to two polychlorinated phenols that uncouple oxidative phosphorylation"],["candidate","raw/41588_2007_BFng1991_MOESM243_ESM.pdf","Supplementary Note","We stress that what follows are associations which must ultimately be verified."],["candidate","raw/41588_2007_BFng1991_MOESM243_ESM.pdf","Supplementary Note","We favor SWH1 and disfavor YAT1 as a candidate for two reasons."],["candidate","raw/41588_2007_BFng1991_MOESM243_ESM.pdf","Supplementary Note","For the QTL hot spots on chromosome 14, there are numerous polymorphic genes"],["candidate","raw/41588_2007_BFng1991_MOESM243_ESM.pdf","Supplementary Note","we favor MKS1 (YNL076W)"],["candidate","raw/41588_2007_BFng1991_MOESM243_ESM.pdf","Supplementary Note","analogous to PHO84, which we verified as the resistance-conferring polymorphism"],["trait","raw/41588_2007_BFng1991_MOESM238_ESM.pdf","Supplementary Table 3 legend","lists individual compound response traits, including SMP concentration"],["trait","raw/41588_2007_BFng1991_MOESM238_ESM.pdf","Supplementary Table 3 legend","a time point (in hours) at which 